                            <comment id="13713833" author="ikelly" created="Fri, 19 Jul 2013 16:51:22 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;What code is it exiting with? Shouldn&apos;t it get the correct code when it calls Bookie#shutdown()?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="13714383" author="rakeshr" created="Sat, 20 Jul 2013 08:17:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Its exiting with &apos;ExitCode.OK&apos; and is masking the actual &apos;ExitCode.ZK_REG_FAIL&apos;, which then added during Bookie#registerBookie fails. &lt;br/&gt;
Could you please execute the test case in the attached patch, it will help us to understand more.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="13718403" author="ikelly" created="Wed, 24 Jul 2013 14:22:23 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Ah, as the bookie hasn&apos;t started at this point, it won&apos;t actually call shutdown() to get the error code. I think this applies to 4.2.2 also.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="13718437" author="ikelly" created="Wed, 24 Jul 2013 14:56:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Committed r1506582 to trunk.&lt;br/&gt;
Committed revision 1506584 to branch-4.2.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Thanks Rakesh.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
